==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|tumour|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|tumor||swelling|lang=la}}, from {{m|la|tumeō||I bulge, swell}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|oncology|pathology|lang=en}} An abnormal [[growth]]; [[differential diagnosis]] includes [[abscess]], [[metaplasia]], and [[neoplasia]].

====Usage notes====
* {{alternative spelling of|tumor|from=British|from2=Australia|from3=New Zealand|from4=Canada||lang=en}}
* {{term|tumour|Tumour|lang=en}} is the standard modern British and Commonwealth spelling (including Canada), and {{term|tumor|lang=en}} is the standard American spelling.

====Derived terms====
* [[tumourigenesis]]

